Absolutely — I’ll only inspect for now and won’t rename, move, or modify anything until you’ve reviewed and approved a plan.

I’ll start by taking a read-only inventory of `~/Pictures`, including folder structure, file types, image/video counts, and possible RAW files.
```bash
cd ~/Pictures && pwd && find . -maxdepth 3 -type f | sed 's#^\./##' | head -200 && echo "---- top-level dirs ----" && find . -maxdepth 1 -type d | sed 's#^\./##' | sort && echo "---- extension counts ----" && find . -type f | awk '
{
  n=split($0,a,"/")
  name=a[n]
  if (name !~ /\./) ext="[no extension]"
  else {
    ext=name
    sub(/^.*\./,"",ext)
    ext=tolower(ext)
  }
  count[ext]++
}
END {
  for (e in count) print count[e], e
}' | sort -nr | head -100
```

